SUMMARY:Ali Wong Live LIVE at McCaw Hall (Aug 13)
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout Ali Wong\nAli Wong is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians of her generation\, known for her fearlessly raw\, hilarious\, and unapologetically honest comedy style. She burst into mainstream consciousness with her Netflix specials Baby Cobra (2016) and Hard Knock Wife (2018)\, both filmed while she was visibly pregnant — a bold and unforgettable choice that became her signature image. \nHer comedy dives deep into marriage\, motherhood\, sex\, race\, and the absurdities of modern life\, delivered with a rapid-fire wit and zero filter. Wong’s ability to make audiences simultaneously cringe and howl with laughter has earned her a devoted global fanbase and critical acclaim across the entertainment industry. \nBeyond stand-up\, Ali Wong has starred in the hit Netflix romantic comedy film Always Be My Maybe (2019)\, the critically acclaimed drama series Beef (2023) — for which she won a Primetime Emmy Award — and has appeared in numerous television and film projects. Her live shows are known for being high-energy\, deeply personal\, and absolutely unforgettable. \nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday\, August 13\, 2026 \nTime: 7:00 PM \nVenue: McCaw Hall\, 321 Mercer Street\, Seattle\, WA 98109 \nTicket Price Range: $59 – $199 \nAge Restrictions: This is an 18+ show. Strong adult language and mature themes throughout. \nAbout McCaw Hall\nMarion Oliver McCaw Hall is one of Seattle’s premier performing arts venues\, located in the heart of the Seattle Center campus — just steps from the iconic Space Needle. The hall is home to the Seattle Opera and Pacific Northwest Ballet\, and regularly hosts world-class comedy\, music\, and special events. \nWith a seating capacity of approximately 2\,900\, McCaw Hall offers excellent sightlines from virtually every seat in the house. The venue features a stunning modern design with state-of-the-art acoustics\, comfortable seating\, and a welcoming atmosphere that makes every performance feel intimate despite its size. \nAmenities include multiple bars and concession areas\, accessible seating options\, and convenient parking in the Seattle Center garage. The surrounding Seattle Center grounds offer great pre-show dining and entertainment options\, making it easy to turn the evening into a full night out. \nWhat to Expect\nAli Wong’s live shows are a masterclass in stand-up comedy — fast-paced\, deeply personal\, and packed with laugh-out-loud moments from start to finish. Expect her signature blend of self-deprecating humor\, sharp social commentary\, and stories about relationships\, family\, and the chaos of everyday life. \nThis is a solo stand-up performance\, so you’ll get the full Ali Wong experience with no distractions. Fans of her Netflix specials will recognize her style but can expect all-new material crafted for this tour. Arrive early to grab a drink\, find your seat\, and soak in the energy of a sold-out crowd ready to laugh. \nShows typically run approximately 75–90 minutes with no intermission. Dress comfortably — this is a casual\, fun night out with one of comedy’s biggest stars. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $59 – $199 (plus applicable fees) \nTickets are available through Ticketmaster (official) and VividSeats (resale marketplace). Resale ticket prices may vary from face value. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/ali-wong-live-at-mccaw-hall-aug-thu/
LOCATION:McCaw Hall\, 321 Mercer Street\, Seattle\, Washington\, 98109\, United States
